    {"id":"p09","number":9,"smallestVersionHours":[8,18],"effortEstimate":"Rough editorial estimate: 8–18 hands-on hours for the smallest version, its checks and brief notes. Assumes the listed preparation and tools are ready; first attempts may take longer. Excludes extensions, installation and waiting for materials. Use the CAD-only option for this range; fabrication can take substantially longer.","title":"A mechanism from requirement to revision","stage":"University design","question":"Can I make one useful motion repeatably?","prerequisites":["CAD basics","Statics/dynamics","Measurement","Safe tool training for physical work"],"minimum":"Write three measurable requirements for a small low-energy mechanism; sketch alternatives, model one and test a key behavior.","extension":"Add an assembly plan, tolerance study and a second revision after test evidence.","costUSD":[0,60],"costBasis":"CAD-only minimum can be free; physical prototype cost is an editable estimate.","tools":["CAD","Drawings","Optional trained maker-space access"],"deliverables":["Requirements","Rejected concept","CAD/drawing","Test record","Revision log"],"verify":"Use the same written test procedure before and after a design change.","stopWhen":"Evidence supports the stated requirements or clearly identifies the remaining failure.","explainWithoutAI":"Why did you reject one alternative and what evidence changed the final design?","themes":["mechanisms","structures","manufacturing"],"sources":["nasa-structures","nasa-systems"],"sourceUse":"Original desktop project."},
    {"id":"p10","number":10,"smallestVersionHours":[12,24],"effortEstimate":"Rough editorial estimate: 12–24 hands-on hours for the smallest version, its checks and brief notes. Assumes the listed preparation and tools are ready; first attempts may take longer. Excludes extensions, installation and waiting for materials. Keep the environment and robot model deliberately small.","title":"A robot that can explain its failure","stage":"University exploration","question":"Can a simulated robot complete a constrained inspection task under uncertainty?","prerequisites":["Programming","Coordinate frames","Controls","Basic probability"],"minimum":"Separate localization, planning and control in a small simulated environment with a measurable goal.","extension":"Introduce one uncertainty at a time, such as noisy position or a blocked path; implement an explicit recovery or stop condition.","costUSD":[0,0],"costBasis":"Simulation-only minimum using existing computer.","tools":["Python or robotics simulator","Version control"],"deliverables":["Architecture diagram","Reproducible scenarios","Success metric","Failure taxonomy"],"verify":"Run nominal, edge and deliberately failing cases; inspect which subsystem failed.","stopWhen":"A documented set of cases produces explainable results, including limits.","explainWithoutAI":"Which part estimates the world, which chooses the route and which executes motion?","themes":["robotics","undersea","gnc"],"sources":["astrobee-code","whoi-engineers"],"sourceUse":"Original simulated project; not a professional autonomy qualification."},
    {"id":"p11","number":11,"smallestVersionHours":[8,16],"effortEstimate":"Rough editorial estimate: 8–16 hands-on hours for the smallest version, its checks and brief notes. Assumes the listed preparation and tools are ready; first attempts may take longer. Excludes extensions, installation and waiting for materials.","title":"Habitat workshop: an integration study","stage":"University integration","question":"Do individually sensible subsystems still work as a whole?","prerequisites":["Basic thermal/resource analysis","Technical writing","One developed technical specialty"],"minimum":"Create a conceptual or simulated robotic workshop with stakeholders, operating modes, interfaces and power/mass/data budgets.","extension":"Introduce an interface mismatch or component failure; revise the concept and verification plan.","costUSD":[0,0],"costBasis":"Conceptual and simulation minimum with existing computer.","tools":["Diagrams","Spreadsheet","Requirements table"],"deliverables":["Concept of operations","Interface document","Resource budgets","Verification matrix","Trade decision"],"verify":"Trace each requirement to a test, analysis, inspection or demonstration; separately ask whether the concept serves the user's need.","stopWhen":"Every key interface has an owner, unit convention and check, and one mismatch has been resolved visibly.","explainWithoutAI":"What is the difference between meeting the written requirement and meeting the actual need?","themes":["systems","life-support","robotics"],"sources":["nasa-systems","nasa-vv"],"sourceUse":"Original conceptual study; does not establish human-spaceflight or economic feasibility."},
    {"id":"p12","number":12,"smallestVersionHours":[6,12],"effortEstimate":"Rough editorial estimate: 6–12 hands-on hours for the smallest version, its checks and brief notes. Assumes the listed preparation and tools are ready; first attempts may take longer. Excludes extensions, installation and waiting for materials. Assumes the earlier project and test evidence already exist.","title":"One portfolio case study worth defending","stage":"Professional launch","question":"Can someone reconstruct my engineering judgment?","prerequisites":["A mature earlier project","Documented test evidence"],"minimum":"Choose one project and explain its problem, constraints, alternatives, model, implementation, tests, revisions and remaining limits.","extension":"Give a short technical presentation and invite a reviewer to reproduce one result.","costUSD":[0,0],"costBasis":"Documentation of existing work; excludes optional new hardware.","tools":["Repository","Readable report","Slides or short demonstration"],"deliverables":["Case study","Reproduction instructions","Test evidence","Contribution statement","Next experiment"],"verify":"Ask another person to reproduce a result without your help and correct the documentation gaps.","stopWhen":"You can explain a failure, defend a decision and distinguish your contribution from team or AI assistance.","explainWithoutAI":"Which conclusion is strongest, and what evidence would make you change it?","themes":["systems","manufacturing","structures"],"sources":["arclab","nasa-systems"],"sourceUse":"Portfolio guidance, not a substitute for the official university capstone."}
